    "result_text": "All 47 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for `POST /api/owners`. When the request supplies a `birthDate` (ISO), the response now returns `ageBand` computed as the completed years between `birthDate` and the owner's effective `registrationDate`: `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+); absent when no `birthDate` is given.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) to `OwnerFields` (the request/DTO), and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` response schema.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `birth_date` column) with getter/setter, so the value survives the create\u2192reload cycle (the test reads it back via a separate `GET`).\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table across all DB variants (tests run on hsqldb).\n- **`rest/function/owner/AgeBand.java`** \u2014 new helper computing the band via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()`, returning `null` when either date is absent.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression deriving `ageBand` from `owner.getBirthDate()` against `owner.getRegistrationDate()`, alongside the existing derived fields.\n\nThe request-body `birthDate` flows into the entity via the existing MapStruct `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` mapping (no pipeline change needed), and `ageBand` is derived purely at response-mapping time \u2014 consistent with the other derived fields (`displayName`, `checkDigit`, `contactPreference`). `Cp34Tests` (birthDate `1990-01-01`, defaulted registrationDate \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, and no existing checkpoint regressed.",
